    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#oghuz-turks">Oghuz Turks</a> from the Central Asian steppe, the Seljuks built an empire from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#khorasan">Khorasan</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and became protectors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sunni-islam">Sunni Islam</a>.</li><li>Their victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#battle-of-manzikert">Manzikert</a> opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#anatolia">Anatolia</a> to Turkish settlement, paving the way for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and helping provoke the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#crusade">Crusades</a>.</li><li>With no fixed succession, the empire splintered after 1092; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#qara-khitai">Qara Khitai</a> and Khwarazmian blows ended the Great Seljuk line by 1194.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The poet and mathematician <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#omar-khayyam">Omar Khayyam</a> worked under Seljuk patronage on the Jalali solar calendar of 1079, more accurate than the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#julian-calendar">Julian calendar</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

